=== Setsusha ===
[[File:Hongu Shrine (Kibitsu Shrine precinct shrine).JPG|right|thumb|200px|{{center|Hongu Shrine}}]]
It is said that in ancient times there were five shrine buildings and 72 subsidiary shrines. The five shrine buildings (Main Shrine, Hongu Shrine, Shingu Shrine, Naiku Shrine, and Iwayama Shrine) are collectively referred to as ``Kibitsu Gosho Daimyojin''. </ref>. {{ill|lt=2025|Q49616|qid=Q49616|1=2025}} ({{ill|lt=Reiwa|Q62609017|qid=Q62609017|1=Reiwa era}}7) Currently, Shingu Shrine and Naiku Shrine are enshrined in Hongu Shrine.
* Hongu Shrine - One of the Gosho Daimyojin shrines. Enshrined deity: {{ill|lt=Emperor Korei|Q313041|qid=Q313041|1=Emperor Kōrei}} (7th generation. Father of Daikibitsuhiko no Mikoto).
** Shingu Shrine - One of the Gosho Daimyojin shrines. Enshrined deity: Kibi Takehiko no Mikoto (son of Wakahiko Kenkibitsu Hiko no Mikoto). Enshrined at Hongu Shrine. It was enshrined in Higashiyama in the south until the end of the Meiji period.
** Naiku Shrine - One of the Gosho Daimyojin shrines. Enshrined deity: Hyakuta Yumiya Hime no Mikoto (wife of Daikibitsuhiko no Mikoto). Enshrined at Hongu Shrine. It was originally enshrined on the mountain in the southern part of {{ill|lt=Kibi Nakayama|Q135646238|qid=Q135646238|1=Mount Kibi no Nakayama}}.
* Sanshagu - A collective term for the following three companies.
** Kasuga Shrine
** Daijingu Shrine
** Hachiman Shrine
* Iwayama Shrine - One of the Gosho Daimyojin shrines. Enshrined deity: Kenhikkatabetsu no Mikoto (landlord deity of Kibi Province).
* Taki Matsuri Shrine
* Ebisusha
*Soreisha Shrine
* Ichidosha
* Uga Shrine - Enshrined on the island of Kamiike.
