=== Cultural assets ===

=== National Treasure ===
* Main shrine and worship hall (attached ridge plate [Meiwa 6], ridge plate [Koka 2]) (building)
*: {{ill|lt=Muromachi period|Q334845|qid=Q334845|1=Muromachi period}}[[wikt:Mid period|Middle period]], constructed in 1997 ({{ill|lt=1425|Q6283|qid=Q6283|1=1425}}). The main shrine and worship hall are designated as one building. {{ill|lt=1902|Q2043|qid=Q2043|1=1902}} ({{ill|lt=Meiji|Q3125096|qid=Q3125096|1=Meiji era}}35th year) On April 17th, it was designated as a special protected building based on the {{ill|lt=Ancient Shrines and Temples Preservation Law|Q11411552|qid=Q11411552|1=Ancient Temples and Shrines Preservation Law}}. Designated as a national treasure on March 29, {{ill|lt=1952|Q5272|qid=Q5272|1=1952}} ({{ill|lt=Showa|Q327567|qid=Q327567|1=Shōwa era}}27) based on {{ill|lt=Cultural Properties Protection Law|Q1188502|qid=Q1188502|1=Cultural Properties Protection Law}}<ref name="Main shrine and worship hall">{{Nationally designated cultural properties database|102|2993|Kibitsu Shrine main shrine and worship hall}}<br />[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=4 Kibitsu Shrine main shrine and worship hall] {{ja icon}} (Okayama prefecture homepage "Okayama cultural assets"). </ref>.

=== Important cultural property (designated by the country) ===
* Minamizuishinmon (building)
*: Built in the 2nd year of Enbun ({{ill|lt=1357|Q6135|qid=Q6135|1=1357}}) during the Muromachi period [[wikt:first half|early]]. {{ill|lt=1911|Q2076|qid=Q2076|1=1911}} ({{ill|lt=Meiji|Q3125096|qid=Q3125096|1=Meiji era}}44) Designated on April 17th<ref name="Minamizuishinmon">{{Nationally designated cultural property database|102|2994|Kibitsu Shrine Minamizuishinmon}}<br />[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=5 Kibitsu Shrine Minami Zuishinmon] {{ja icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage "Okayama Cultural Properties"). </ref>.
* Hokuzuishinmon (building)
*: Built in the 12th year of Tenbun ({{ill|lt=1543|Q6523|qid=Q6523|1=1543}}) during the Muromachi period [[wikt:late|late]]. {{ill|lt=1913|Q2080|qid=Q2080|1=1913}} ({{ill|lt=Taisho|Q329174|qid=Q329174|1=Taishō era}}2) Designated on April 14th<ref name="Kitazuishinmon">{{National designated cultural property database|102|2995|Kibitsu Shrine Kitazuijinmon}}<br />[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=6 Kibitsu Shrine Kitazuishinmon] {{ja icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage "Okayama Cultural Properties"). </ref>.
* Okamaden (building)*: Constructed in {{ill|lt=Edo period|Q184963|qid=Q184963|1=Edo period}}, {{ill|lt=Keicho|Q1328185|qid=Q1328185|1=Keichō}}17 ({{ill|lt=1612|Q6771|qid=Q6771|1=1612}}). {{ill|lt=1980|Q2439|qid=Q2439|1=1980}} Designated on January 26, 1972<ref name="Okama-dono">{{Nationally designated cultural properties database|102|2996|Kibitsu Shrine Okama-dono}}<br />[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=7 Kibitsu Shrine Okamaden] {{ja icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage "Okayama Cultural Properties"). </ref>.
* 1 pair of wooden lion guardian dogs (sculpture)
*: Created from the late {{ill|lt=Kamakura period|Q236205|qid=Q236205|1=Kamakura period}} period to the Nanbokucho period. It is enshrined on the east and west sides of the inner hall of the main shrine. {{ill|lt=2002|Q1987|qid=Q1987|1=2002}} ({{ill|lt=Heisei|Q234510|qid=Q234510|1=Heisei era}}14) Designated on June 26th<ref>{{Nationally designated cultural properties database|201|10545|Wooden lion guardian dog}}<br />[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=518 Wooden lion guardian dog] {{ja icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage "Okayama Cultural Properties"). </ref>.

=== Important intangible folk cultural property (designated by the country) ===
* {{ill|lt=Bicchu Kagura|Q11387313|qid=Q11387313|1=Bichu Kagura}}
*: Kagura dedicated throughout the Bitchu region, and performed at Kibitsu Shrine on the 10th of every month. The preservation organization is the Bitchu Kagura Preservation Society. Designated on February 3, 1979 icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage “Okayama Cultural Properties”). </ref>.

=== Okayama prefecture designated cultural property ===
* Important cultural property (tangible cultural property)
** Corridor (building) - Constructed during the Sengoku period and the Tensho era ({{ill|lt=1573|Q6678|qid=Q6678|1=1573}} - {{ill|lt=1591|Q6766|qid=Q6766|1=1591}}). {{ill|lt=1976|Q2480|qid=Q2480|1=1976}} Designated on March 27, 1976. </ref>.
** Odachi inscribed by Hideyuki Osafune (craft) - Muromachi period, Choroku 3 ({{ill|lt=1459|Q6524|qid=Q6524|1=1459}}). Deposited at Okayama Prefectural Museum. {{ill|lt=1982|Q2436|qid=Q2436|1=1982}} Designated on April 9, 1982 <ref>[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=700 Odachi, inscribed Bishū Osafune Hideyuki] {{ja icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage "Okayama Cultural Properties"). </ref>. Blade length 127.2 cm, warp 3.9 cm. Kizukuri, hermitage building. Hideyuki is a representative figure among the {{ill|lt=Osafune school|Q11653605|qid=Q11653605|1=Osafune school}} branch of swordsmiths called the Kowarari school.** Odachi Norimitsu (craft) - Made in the Muromachi period, Bun'an 3 ({{ill|lt=1446|Q6430|qid=Q6430|1=1446}}). Deposited at {{ill|lt=Okayama Prefectural Museum|Q3247162|qid=Q3247162|1=Okayama Prefectural Museum}}. {{ill|lt=1994|Q2067|qid=Q2067|1=1994}} Designated on April 5, 1994 <ref>[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=701 Odachi Norimitsu] {{ja icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage "Okayama Cultural Properties"). </ref>. Total length 377.3 cm, blade length 226.7 cm, warp 5 cm, weight 13 kg. Hog-zukuri, round building. The largest Japanese sword in Japan during the Koto period. Although there is no evidence that it was used as a votive sword, the entire blade is hardened, the {{ill|lt=stem (sword)|Q1963918|qid=Q1963918|lt=stem|1=nakago}} is long, and the three mekugi holes are evenly spaced, indicating that it was made with actual combat in mind.
** Gyodo mask (craft) - Deposited at Okayama Prefectural Museum. {{ill|lt=1959|Q5302|qid=Q5302|1=1959}} (Showa 34) Designated on March 27th <ref>[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=699 Gyodo-men] {{ja icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage "Okayama Cultural Properties"). </ref>.** Goryeo version of All Sutras (calligraphs/scriptures) - Korean scriptures of {{ill|lt=Koryo|Q28208|qid=Q28208|1=Goryeo}}{{ill|lt=period|Q11514315|qid=Q11514315|1=Historical period}}. Designated on March 27, 1959 (Showa 34) <ref>[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=594 Goryeo version of all sutras] {{ja icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage "Okayama Cultural Properties"). </ref>.
** Paper-backed sumi-sho renga (calligraphy/scripture) - A collection of haiku from the Horaku renga performed at Kibitsu Shrine in the 8th year of Oei ({{ill|lt=1401|Q6110|qid=Q6110|1=1401}}). Designated on March 27, 1959 (Showa 34) <ref>[http://www.pref.okayama.jp/cgi-bin/bunka/culture/controller/client/resultDetail.cgi?id=764 Honsokusho Renga] {{ja icon}} (Okayama Prefecture homepage "Cultural Properties of Okayama"). </ref>.
* Intangible folk cultural assets
** Imperial House Dance - Held on {{ill|lt=July 31st|Q2715|qid=Q2715|1=July 31}} in the Imperial Palace district of Monzen-cho. Designated on March 27, 1959. </ref>.

=== Damage ===
* {{ill|lt=2021|Q49628|qid=Q49628|1=2021}} ({{ill|lt=Reiwa|Q62609017|qid=Q62609017|1=Reiwa era}}3) From January 15th to 22nd, it was discovered that someone had made linear scratches on the pillars of the shrine's worship hall and corridor. In February of the same year, a suspect who had damaged {{ill|lt=Matsuyama Castle|Q981357|qid=Q981357|1=Matsuyama Castle (Iyo)}} and {{ill|lt=Kochi Castle|Q1012815|qid=Q1012815|1=Kōchi Castle}} was arrested for violating {{ill|lt=Cultural Properties Protection Act|Q1188502|qid=Q1188502|1=Cultural Properties Protection Law}}, and was arrested again for committing similar crimes at Kibitsu Shrine.<ref>{{Cite web|Japanese book|date=2021-02-13 |url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210213122041/https://www.jiji.com/jc/article?k=2021021300375&g=soc |title=Rearrest of 47-year-old man suspected of damaging Kibitsu Shrine - Okayama Prefectural Police |website=Jiji Press|publisher=Jiji Press|accessdate=2021-02-13}} {{ja icon}}</ref>.

